{"name":"Berry Blue","hex":"#32607a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Berry Blue","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A purplish-blue color resembling that of blueberries"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purplish-blue colour resembling that of blueberries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Berry_Blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jell-O","blocks":[{"text":"Jell-O is an American brand offering a variety of powdered gelatin dessert, pudding, and no-bake cream pie mixes. The original gelatin dessert is the signature of the brand. \"Jell-O\" is a registered trademark of Kraft Heinz, and is based in Chicago, Illinois."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/2019-10-10_22_15_43_Gelatin_from_a_single_opened_cup_of_Jell-O_strawberry_gelatin_snack_being_lifted_by_a_spoon_in_the_Franklin_Farm_section_of_Oak_Hill%2C_Fairfax_County%2C_Virginia.jpg/330px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jell-O"},{"title":"Pebbles (cereal)","blocks":[{"text":"Pebbles is a brand of breakfast cereal which was introduced in the United States by Post Consumer Brands on October 20, 1971 featuring characters from the animated series The Flintstones as spokestoons. The product line includes multiple varieties with the two most popular being Cocoa Pebbles and Fruity Pebbles."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/62/Pebbles_cereal_brand_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pebbles_(cereal)"},{"title":"Berry","blocks":[{"text":"A berry is a small, pulpy, and often edible fruit. Typically, berries are juicy, rounded, brightly colored, sweet, sour or tart, and do not have a stone or pit although many pips or seeds may be present.‍ Common examples of berries in the culinary sense are strawberries, raspberries, blueberries, blackberries, white currants, blackcurrants, and redcurrants.‍ In Britain, soft fruit is a horticultural term for such fruits.‍"}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Berberis_thunbergii_berries.jpg/330px-Berberis_thunbergii_berries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berry"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Pearl_bixby_wait.jpg/500px-Pearl_bixby_wait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Pearl_bixby_wait.jpg/1280px-Pearl_bixby_wait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Pearl_bixby_wait.jpg/500px-Pearl_bixby_wait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APearl_bixby_wait.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/St._Nicholas_%28serial%29_%28187